  "summary": "I wrote src/main.ts, and it passes typecheck. I haven't run `vite build` or loaded it in a browser, so the rendering and shadows are unchecked. The scene has a 260×260 ground plane and three instanced draws: 8,000 trunks, 8,000 canopies (cones) and 2,000 rocks (squashed spheres). Positions come from a seeded LCG, so the forest is the same on every load. Canopies and rocks each get a per-instance HSL colour. A shadow-casting directional light, a hemisphere light and exponential fog (density 0.0045) light the scene. The orbit camera uses `autoRotate: 0.12` and sits at [0, 85, 130], which should keep the whole 65-unit-radius forest in view. I assumed `autoRotate` is a slow rotation rate in rad/s. `window.__EVAL_READY__` is set on the second frame callback, and again on a `requestAnimationFrame` after `app.ready()`.",
